      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-30 11:06:23",
      "type": "原文",
      "type_label": "原文",
      "text": "AI may well be able to write massive software projects “from scratch”, but that almost certainly isn’t the fastest / highest performance / highest security / most token efficient way to do things. Good building blocks matter.\n\nIn addition to RL’ing the agents on final task loss, we should try to get them to regularize the building blocks as well. What would the standard library look like that makes the agents most effective?\n\nIt is likely at the limit that it turns out to be some alien organization of code, but given the existing human-bias in training, I bet that in the near term it would be lovely code that old programmers would appreciate.\n\nI suspect the same could be said for mathematics, but that is out of my lane.",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": null,
      "reply_to": "",
      "engagement": {},
      "url": "https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2116003755078381762",
      "images": [],
      "media": [],
      "enriched": false
    },
