      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "SpaceX is accusing T-Mobile and other legacy carriers of deliberately trying to harm the company and undermine @Starlink Mobile's expansion by pushing outdated, restrictive satellite-to-phone rules that could prevent millions of people in underserved communities from accessing the service.\n\n\"SpaceX has worked extensively with other operators, including T-Mobile. Unfortunately, the misplaced desire to harm a competitor has led many incumbents to oppose modernized rules that would bring direct-to-cell service to underserved border communities. The Commission should recognize that AFTRCC is now purely a lobbying organization whose mission is to protect legacy companies and their comments should not be viewed as independent or objective,\" SpaceX said in a new filing to the FCC.\n\nFull filing in thread below:",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "SawyerMerritt",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1837744842715082752/xH9vYixL_200x200.jpg",
        "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-30 02:51:51",
